  {
    id: 'gf2',
    title: '剪纸工作坊',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 8,
    text: 'Every Saturday morning, a small room above the tea shop near my school fills with the sound of scissors. It is ___1___ workshop where Ms. Zhou, a retired teacher, teaches paper cutting to young people. She started the class five years ago after noticing that ___2___ (few) students than before showed interest in the old patterns. In her view, a piece of red paper and a pair of scissors are all that ___3___ (need) to tell a story in a picture. Students first learn to draw the pattern lightly on the paper, and then cut along the line ___4___ (care). The hardest part, ___5___ the two shapes are joined by a single thin line, must be left until the end of the work. Ms. Zhou also asks her students ___6___ (collect) old patterns from their grandparents, because many designs were never written ___7___ and are dying out with the artists who made them. Last month, the works from her class ___8___ (show) in the city museum, and hundreds of visitors stopped to take photos of those thin red lines. One student said the class had taught her more patience than all the textbook ___9___ (page). Ms. Zhou now plans a second class for the summer holiday, hoping ___10___ (keep) this tradition alive in a city that changes too fast.',
    answers: [
      { n: 1, answer: 'a', explain: '泛指“一间工作坊”，workshop 以辅音音素开头，用不定冠词 a。' },
      { n: 2, answer: 'fewer', give: 'few', explain: '后面有 than before，要用比较级；students 是可数名词，few 变 fewer。' },
      { n: 3, answer: 'is needed', give: 'need', explain: 'all that is needed 是固定说法，that 指代 all，从句谓语用单数，且与 need 是被动关系。' },
      { n: 4, answer: 'carefully', give: 'care', explain: '修饰动词 cut 要用副词，形容词 careful 变 carefully。' },
      { n: 5, answer: 'where', explain: '先行词 part 表示抽象地点，非限制性定语从句结构完整、缺地点状语，用 where。' },
      { n: 6, answer: 'to collect', give: 'collect', explain: 'ask sb to do sth，要求某人做某事时用不定式作宾语补足语。' },
      { n: 7, answer: 'down', explain: 'write down“记录下来”是固定搭配，缺副词 down。' },
      { n: 8, answer: 'were shown', give: 'show', explain: '主语 the works 与 show 是被动关系，Last month 决定用一般过去时的被动语态。' },
      { n: 9, answer: 'pages', give: 'page', explain: 'all the textbook 后接可数名词复数，page 变 pages。' },
      { n: 10, answer: 'to keep', give: 'keep', explain: 'hope to do sth，希望做某事用不定式作宾语。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'gf3',
    title: '屋顶气象站',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 9,
    text: 'Two years ago, our physics club put a small weather station on the roof of the teaching building. At first we only recorded the temperature, but our teacher suggested collecting ___1___ (vary) kinds of data, because a single number tells us little. Now the readings for wind, rainfall and air quality ___2___ (update) online every ten minutes, and anyone can open the page and see ___3___ the weather was like an hour ago. The most useful part is not the machine but the weekly report, ___4___ we compare our numbers with the official ones from the city station. Last autumn our report showed that the playground was nearly four degrees hotter than the shaded area behind the library, ___5___ finding that surprised our geography teacher. She explained that the hard surface of the playground ___6___ (absorb) more heat than soil and grass do. Since then the student union ___7___ (raise) money for twenty young trees, and they were put along the wall last weekend so that the biology garden can get ___8___ (exact) the right amount of shade. Several members have even decided ___9___ (study) meteorology at university. It shows that curiosity and careful records ___10___ turn a school roof into a real laboratory.',
    answers: [
      { n: 1, answer: 'various', give: 'vary', explain: '修饰名词 kinds 要用形容词，动词 vary 变 various。' },
      { n: 2, answer: 'are updated', give: 'update', explain: 'readings 与 update 是被动关系，every ten minutes 表经常发生，用一般现在时的被动。' },
      { n: 3, answer: 'what', explain: 'see 的宾语从句里 like 缺宾语，用 what 表示“什么样的天气”。' },
      { n: 4, answer: 'where', explain: '先行词 report 表示抽象场合，从句不缺主语或宾语，只缺地点状语，用 where。' },
      { n: 5, answer: 'a', explain: '泛指“一个令人惊讶的发现”，finding 是可数名词且以辅音音素开头。' },
      { n: 6, answer: 'absorbs', give: 'absorb', explain: '讲科学道理用一般现在时，主语 the hard surface 是单数，动词加 -s。' },
      { n: 7, answer: 'has raised', give: 'raise', explain: 'since then 与现在完成时连用，the student union 看作一个整体，谓语用单数。' },
      { n: 8, answer: 'exactly', give: 'exact', explain: '修饰 the right amount 用副词，表示“恰好是合适的量”。' },
      { n: 9, answer: 'to study', give: 'study', explain: 'decide to do sth，决定做某事用不定式。' },
      { n: 10, answer: 'can', explain: '句子缺谓语动词，结合句意“能够让屋顶变成实验室”填情态动词 can（will 亦通）。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'gf4',
    title: '睡眠与成绩',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 8,
    text: 'Most people believe that sleeping less and drinking more coffee is a smart way to prepare for an exam. School doctors in our city ___1___ (warn) students against this habit for years. “The brain files what you have learned while you sleep,” one doctor explained at our school last week. “Cut your sleep, and you cut the ___2___ (able) to remember.” Her advice sounds simple, yet few students follow it. A survey of 800 senior students, ___3___ (carry) out last March, showed that more than half of them went to bed after midnight and that the students who slept least did ___4___ (bad) in the morning tests than those who slept eight hours. Lack of sleep is not the only cause of tiredness. Sitting for four hours a day also weakens the heart and the muscles, so doctors suggest ___5___ (take) a ten-minute walk between classes, ___6___ is something most students never do. Getting enough sleep and moving every day are not luxuries; they are the ___7___ (base) of learning. If schools want students to do better, they should begin ___8___ shortening the school day and by giving PE lessons back. A student who is awake ___9___ the time of an exam can use everything he has learned, while a tired student cannot, no matter how hard he ___10___ (work) during the day.',
    answers: [
      { n: 1, answer: 'have warned', give: 'warn', explain: 'for years 与现在完成时连用，主语 School doctors 是复数。' },
      { n: 2, answer: 'ability', give: 'able', explain: 'the ability to do sth“做某事的能力”，形容词 able 变名词 ability。' },
      { n: 3, answer: 'carried', give: 'carry', explain: '句子谓语是 showed，这里用过去分词作后置定语，survey 与 carry out 是被动关系。' },
      { n: 4, answer: 'worse', give: 'bad', explain: '后文有 than those who slept eight hours，两组比较用比较级；bad 的比较级是 worse。' },
      { n: 5, answer: 'taking', give: 'take', explain: 'suggest 后接动名词作宾语，suggest doing sth。' },
      { n: 6, answer: 'which', explain: '非限制性定语从句指代“医生建议课间散步”这件事，关系词用 which。' },
      { n: 7, answer: 'basis', give: 'base', explain: 'the basis of“……的基础”，这里需要名词 basis。' },
      { n: 8, answer: 'by', explain: 'begin by doing sth“先以做……的方式开始”，与后文的 and by giving 呼应。' },
      { n: 9, answer: 'at', explain: 'at the time of“在……的时候”是固定介词搭配。' },
      { n: 10, answer: 'works', give: 'work', explain: 'no matter how 引导的让步状语从句用一般现在时，主语 he 用第三人称单数。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'gf5',
    title: '跟随父亲上班的一天',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 9,
    text: 'For one day each autumn, Grade 11 students in our school follow a working adult for eight hours. My father agreed ___1___ (be) my host, and I spent the day at a bus repair centre outside the city. I had always thought the work boring; by the end of the day I saw ___2___ in a new light. The first task was to find out why a bus engine had stopped ___3___ (work). Nobody touched a tool at first. They read the error log together and argued quietly about the possible causes. What surprised me most was ___4___ much mathematics the job used, and ___5___ the senior worker explained the same rule three times without losing his temper. Lunch was eaten standing up, ___6___ was the only rest of the morning. In the afternoon I held a torch and passed tools, and twice I handed the wrong one. Instead of shouting, the technician simply asked me to look at the number again. Before leaving, I had to write a short report ___7___ (describe) the process, which was harder than the work itself. The school read out the best reports at ___8___ meeting, and many students now ask their parents about their jobs for ___9___ first time. One day in a real workplace can do a student more good than a month of lectures: it makes the future feel close enough ___10___ (touch).',
    answers: [
      { n: 1, answer: 'to be', give: 'be', explain: 'agree to do sth，同意做某事用不定式作宾语。' },
      { n: 2, answer: 'it', explain: 'see it in a new light“用新的眼光看待它”，it 指代上文的 the work，即父亲的这份工作。' },
      { n: 3, answer: 'working', give: 'work', explain: 'stop doing sth 表示“停止正在做的事”，这里指发动机不再运转。' },
      { n: 4, answer: 'how', explain: '修饰 much 用 how，引导表语从句，表示“多少”。' },
      { n: 5, answer: 'that', explain: '与前面 how 引导的从句并列作表语，该从句结构完整，用 that 引导且不能省略。' },
      { n: 6, answer: 'which', explain: '非限制性定语从句指代“站着吃午饭”这件事，用 which。' },
      { n: 7, answer: 'describing', give: 'describe', explain: 'report 与 describe 是主动关系，用现在分词作后置定语。' },
      { n: 8, answer: 'a', explain: '泛指“一次集会”，at a meeting，meeting 以辅音音素开头。' },
      { n: 9, answer: 'the', explain: 'for the first time“第一次”是固定搭配，序数词前用 the。' },
      { n: 10, answer: 'to touch', give: 'touch', explain: 'enough 用于形容词后时接不定式，close enough to do sth。' },
    ],
